  "tagline": "Log-structured, embeddable key-value engine in pure Rust with keyspaces and transactions.",
  "description": "Fjall is an LSM-tree based embedded key-value store written in safe Rust, positioned as a RocksDB-style engine for the Rust ecosystem without C++ dependencies. It organises data into keyspaces (similar to column families) that share a journal for atomic cross-keyspace writes, offers optional single-writer or optimistic serializable transactions, key-value separation for large blobs, and LZ4 compression. Version 3 shipped in 2026 and releases are frequent. It suits write-heavy Rust applications; for read-mostly workloads a B-tree like redb may be simpler.",
